  "caveats": [
    "m_rings=2 exercises one packing operator (r=0, u=0 => k=d+1, B^0) per instance; the coset-structure question is insensitive to the particular (k, u) beyond the signed-permutation shape.",
    "Toy dimensions (d <= 128): a negative result does not prove the n=2048 instance safe; it falsifies structural shortcuts that would already appear at this scale (rank defects, reduced blocksize requirement, shifted success crossover).",
    "Success fraction is measured against the secret known to the experiment; the attack itself is keyless.",
    "BKZ blocksize 15 and LLL are far weaker than the beta ~ 350 reduction required at production parameters; absolute numbers do not extrapolate."
